{
  "rule": "A block quote at the DOCUMENT ROOT whose first physical source line is a GitHub Alerts marker (`> [!NOTE]` / `[!TIP]` / `[!IMPORTANT]` / `[!WARNING]` / `[!CAUTION]`, ASCII case-insensitive, RENDERER_PIPELINE_VERSION 1.2.0+) is retyped to `crowiAlert{variant}` with a fixed `data.hName: 'blockquote'` hint. The child subtree is NEVER rewritten: the literal marker text and the delimiter `break` stay in the stored AST, so every consumer that does not know `crowiAlert` keeps rendering exactly today's block quote. Anything else — an unknown token, a marker sharing its line with body text, an escaped/entity opening bracket, a marker with no renderable body, a marker below the document root — stays an ordinary blockquote.",
  "why": "`crowiAlert` is the one Crowi-owned node deliberately kept OUT of RENDERED_AST_NODE_DEFS: the `X-Crowi-Ast-Version: 1` union is closed and already has shipped native decoders, so the wire contract this corpus fixes is two-sided — the stored bare shape (producer) AND the ordinary `blockquote` a declared v1 client receives instead of a new discriminant (consumer). Pinning both directions is what makes 'no native code change is required for 1.2.0' a checkable claim rather than an assertion.",
  "consumers": [
    "packages/api/src/renderer/golden-corpus.test.ts",
    "apps/apple/CrowiKit/Tests/CrowiKitTests/RenderedAstGoldenCorpusTests.swift"
  ],
  "consumerContract": "The api jest driver asserts the PRODUCER side (markdown -> expectedAst via runPipeline with an empty registry, and expectedAst -> expectedEnvelope via sanitizeAst). For THIS file the CrowiKit XCTest asserts only its strict envelope decoder over expectedEnvelope and the decode round-trip; the sanitize-walker mirror over expectedAst is deliberately out of scope. `crowiAlert` is a server-only projection that sanitizeAst narrows to a standard blockquote, so a consumer walker cannot reproduce expectedEnvelope from expectedAst — it sees the stored shape as an unknown type and unwraps it, blockquote shell included. The exclusion is by design rather than a coverage gap: no runtime path delivers the stored shape to a client, so asserting the mirror here would assert a path that does not exist. The Swift consumer is wired up in Phase 4 (apps/apple lives on the feature-ios-app/impl branch).",
  "consumerCoordination": "`crowiAlert` never reaches a declared v1 client — `sanitize-ast.ts` narrows it to the ordinary `blockquote` pinned in expectedEnvelope, marker text and delimiter break included — so CrowiKit needs NO code change to keep rendering these pages under pipeline 1.2.0. The release owner hands this fixture plus that contract to the CrowiKit owner before the api release and records the target release branch's existing RenderedAstGoldenCorpusTests run in the release checklist. A native alert rendering needs v2 / capability negotiation and is a separate feature.",
  "normalization": "none — expected values are exact.",
  "exclusions": "Plugin-dispatch output byte strings (Mermaid / PlantUML / link-card / shiki generated HTML) are deliberately NOT pinned by this corpus — packages/e2e/tests/renderer-plugins.spec.ts owns that coverage against a live server. The RENDERED output of these ASTs is likewise out of scope on both sides: this driver never runs `mdast-util-to-hast`, so the callout DOM (and the fallback block quote an alert-unaware web bundle draws from `data.hName`) is pinned by packages/web/src/components/editor/render-mdast.test.tsx instead.",
